<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="Path Traversal">
  <data key="d0">Path Traversal</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">Security vulnerability allowing an attacker to reach files outside the web document root via manipulated path input.&lt;SEP&gt;An action that uses input fields to modify a file path with sequences that traverse to unintended directories.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness in file access logic that allows unauthorized browsing of system directories.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class where user-controlled input is interpreted as a file path by server-side logic, allowing access to arbitrary files.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2efb3aacf8e172b84b6e1793e84eff76-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2efb3aacf8e172b84b6e1793e84eff76-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2efb3aacf8e172b84b6e1793e84eff76-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-294b9877be94f50d0e74d0aa6ca0627b-chunk-000</data>
