<node id="Input Validation">
  <data key="d0">Input Validation</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">Input Validation is a security control mechanism designed to verify user-submitted data against expected format, length, type, or allow-list constraints to prevent malicious data from entering application processing flows. It is generally implemented on the server side as a mechanism to filter, sanitize, or restrict user input before it is used in file operations or backend processing. Critical functions include ensuring input conforms to valid parameters and formats, verifying that all required request fields are present and logically valid, and rejecting data that contains path traversal or other types of malicious characters. This measure acts as a barrier against injection attacks, including stored cross-site scripting (XSS), which can occur if input is not properly sanitized before storage or display. By enforcing these constraints, input validation reduces the risk of data corruption, unauthorized access, and exploitation of application vulnerabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;A security mechanism or practice requiring strict rejection or sanitization of input containing control characters like `\r` and `\n` before use in headers.&lt;SEP&gt;A target mechanism designed to reject or sanitize user-supplied input before including it in application output.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2efb3aacf8e172b84b6e1793e84eff76-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3f4f5cff505f73ed00fb5bb4eebf4557-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-40abae0a95ecce566511731ae40acbbf-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3be59af692385f8910776899901b815f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3145270b6ffe0fd7611c4610be0770a9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b71020ce840e0a943e1deda0b9f2c41-chunk-002</data>
