<node id="SMB Sharing (Server Message Block)">
  <data key="d0">SMB Sharing (Server Message Block)</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A network protocol used to provide shared access to files, printers, and serial ports upon discovery of accessible shares, often leveraged for UNC path attacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2efb3aacf8e172b84b6e1793e84eff76-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-01-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785416397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Remote Credentials Harvesting">
  <data key="d0">Remote Credentials Harvesting</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackGoal</data>
  <data key="d2">The strategic objective to capture stored credentials from a server or service for subsequent privilege escalation or unauthorized access.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2efb3aacf8e172b84b6e1793e84eff76-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-01-methodology.md</data>
