<node id="Input Validation Failure">
  <data key="d0">Input Validation Failure</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Flaw in application logic where user-supplied input is not properly sanitized or encoded before being reflected in responses.&lt;SEP&gt;A known vulnerability type where the application fails to verify or sanitize user provided input before using it in queries.&lt;SEP&gt;The failure of an application to check or filter user supplied data before using it in database interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Failure of an application to validate or escape user-supplied inputs before processing them in SQL queries.&lt;SEP&gt;A flaw in the target where user input containing SSI directives is accepted and executed instead of being rejected or sanitized.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where input handling lacks proper sanitization, allowing injection attempts to reach mail server protocols.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition where user input is not properly sanitized or validated before being used in object assignment or merge operations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-9a2a918bb83307307b4812469ae0001c-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e673fd83bcb14789984668dec20fbae1-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e673fd83bcb14789984668dec20fbae1-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b6a59d6cd5ba7ef78db34ebfda033db4-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8572f501a826eda55dfbb3563ca66b07-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-913dbc8a4681245bade3cc137a3a5962-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0afc271ddfef476dba107d5eebef758e-chunk-002</data>
