<node id="SQL Injection">
  <data key="d0">SQL Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">SQL Injection is a critical security weakness class within the injection family that predominantly affects web applications. It occurs when an application fails to validate, sanitize, or properly parameterize user-supplied input before incorporating it into SQL queries. Attackers exploit this flaw by injecting malicious SQL syntax into backend queries via unsanitized input fields, causing the input to be misinterpreted as legitimate database commands. This vulnerability allows unauthorized database access, modification, or deletion of sensitive data, with strategic outcomes ranging from unauthorized retrieval to privilege escalation and bypassing of authentication checks. At its core, SQL Injection represents a weakness in input handling that permits the execution of arbitrary SQL statements, enabling attackers to manipulate backend databases without proper authorization. Commonly, such issues arise from concatenating untrusted data directly into dynamic SQL queries without adequate validation mechanisms or sufficient sanitization techniques. As a widely known attack method, it poses significant risks to data integrity and confidentiality, making proper input handling essential for prevention.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d8f69c7e813a7c5f87c603a15e656cb8-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5f4e64e8a4e13f14c3ff3f3f15491570-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-31756ff9be064b82f25dbfbf1263059b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-31756ff9be064b82f25dbfbf1263059b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3057c5214ae12e7effb35fb90f29a423-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d2ff4b7186c17bdc52457e2c1f1dc3fe-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d49f15f997dc4e5a62d377e48dacdb8e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-df80c9fe91c3765dc83d86ba6565a823-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e673fd83bcb14789984668dec20fbae1-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e673fd83bcb14789984668dec20fbae1-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7a6169ed7611988c7689307fbb72ef84-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ea8988b320818e8e44a6d07527492e35-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b515367113bce44cf3564abc5019508d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a94663073c0acb859206ca0011ed60dc-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-05-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-apit-99-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athn-04-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athn-11-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-2-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-3-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-7-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-05-8-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-inpv-14-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-10-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785584144</data>
