  <data key="d2">A testing action that sends crafted input designed to execute system commands on the target server.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class in input validation where user input is passed to an operating system command without sanitization.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where user input is misused to execute arbitrary operating system commands or operators on the server.&lt;SEP&gt;A technique where an attacker injects malicious OS commands into web application input fields to compromise the server.&lt;SEP&gt;The unauthorized ability to inject and execute arbitrary operating system commands through an application's input validation failure.&lt;SEP&gt;An injection technique that submits malicious system commands via unsanitized input to perform unauthorized actions.</data>
