<node id="Web Server">
  <data key="d0">Web Server</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Web Server is a server software or hardware system designed to host and serve web applications over the internet. It is responsible for receiving HTTP and HTTPS requests from clients, interpreting these requests, and returning appropriate web content such as HTML, images, or other data. Configurations commonly include various web server software such as nginx and Apache, which determine request handling based on file extensions and applied technologies. As the front-end component within the web architecture, it communicates with backend systems and services such as the PL/SQL Gateway layer to process requests and generate responses, ultimately acting as the target system subject to activities like fingerprinting and information gathering.&lt;SEP&gt;The server software running the web application, whose type can be determined via fingerprinting or configuration files to assess SSI capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Host system responsible for serving web pages and interpreting SSI directives if configured to do so.&lt;SEP&gt;An HTTP server that processes web requests and acts as the target of host header injection tests.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-eff998e21395157f6ed4ce495ef006aa-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-eff998e21395157f6ed4ce495ef006aa-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5d55d44f25265c54469eaa8333ead2a4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-5d55d44f25265c54469eaa8333ead2a4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4fc774259228cd414282425d0a281e37-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-4fc774259228cd414282425d0a281e37-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92b67b99fc7587fc9af9d2208dfa4918-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-79636d7f9a295c3fa17a27c773d950df-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-af827feaaf7735b8242b6a751ee616fa-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1fdc50b475aa40c6258b79abf9a867a6-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d49f15f997dc4e5a62d377e48dacdb8e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8572f501a826eda55dfbb3563ca66b07-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8572f501a826eda55dfbb3563ca66b07-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e4ddd30d9c938d44180c61ca6f42e47f-chunk-001</data>
