<node id="Brute Force Attack">
  <data key="d0">Brute Force Attack</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackGoal</data>
  <data key="d2">An attack methodology using repeated guesses of authentication inputs (such as passwords) to gain unauthorized access.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing method using repeated guesses of user credentials or security questions to gain unauthorized access.&lt;SEP&gt;An automated technique that systematically submits many password guesses until a valid credential is found.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing action that involves systematically generating and submitting numerous candidate answers to guess security question responses.&lt;SEP&gt;An iterative password guessing technique used after failing authentication attempts on an administrative interface.&lt;SEP&gt;Goal to obtain valid credentials by testing many username/password pairs.&lt;SEP&gt;A systematic method of testing a range of username and password combinations to gain unauthorized access.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f56c9dfd36da3c20bd6a449315c7cd44-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f56c9dfd36da3c20bd6a449315c7cd44-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-117449b3898c46f40eb1a6ade4a7d591-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001ecd8aa1d653a3601526cc957ea31d-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7e4dbed88f64fa7cde685ea3eeba6062-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92b67b99fc7587fc9af9d2208dfa4918-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-92b67b99fc7587fc9af9d2208dfa4918-chunk-003</data>
