<node id="Authorization Code">
  <data key="d0">Authorization Code</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Authorization Code is a temporary credential issued by the authorization server following successful user consent and authorization request. It is short-lived and is specifically utilized once within the OAuth authorization flow. The primary purpose of this temporary code is to facilitate the exchange for an access token at the token endpoint. This mechanism is prevalent across confidential and public clients alike, ensuring secure proxying of user consent by preventing the client application from directly accessing the user's credentials or resources.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-2-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494597</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Refresh Token">
  <data key="d0">Refresh Token</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A credential that can be used to obtain new access tokens beyond the initial authorization; must be validated against its lifetime.&lt;SEP&gt;A long-lived token used to obtain new access tokens when they expire.&lt;SEP&gt;A long-lived credential used to obtain new access tokens without re-authenticating the user.&lt;SEP&gt;A token issued by the authorization server that enables the client to obtain new access tokens without user re-authentication.&lt;SEP&gt;A long-lived credential used to obtain new access tokens without prompting the user for credentials again.&lt;SEP&gt;A credential issued by the Authorization Server that clients use to obtain a new access token when the current one expires.&lt;SEP&gt;A temporary token provided by the authorization server to allow clients to refresh an expired access token.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-2-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authorization Server (AS)">
  <data key="d0">Authorization Server (AS)</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">OAuth authorization server responsible for granting client access to resources based on user permissions.&lt;SEP&gt;The server component responsible for issuing and validating OAuth tokens, including authorization codes and refresh tokens.&lt;SEP&gt;The server responsible for issuing OAuth tokens to clients after successful user authentication.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-2-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PKCE Extension">
  <data key="d0">PKCE Extension</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A mechanism that secures the authorization code and token exchange by introducing a code_verifier/verifier pair to prevent authorization code token interception and replay.&lt;SEP&gt;A security extension used to secure OAuth flows by providing a code verifier and challenge to prevent authorization code interception.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-006</data>
