  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Authorization Code Flow">
  <data key="d0">Authorization Code Flow</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">OAuth protocol variant used in the example scenario, specifically focusing on authorization codes and the PKCE extension.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific OAuth 2.0 grant type that exchanges authorization codes for access tokens without revealing credentials to the client.&lt;SEP&gt;A weaker security model or comparative baseline in OAuth flows used for evaluation; tokens are never leaked through the initial response to the client.&lt;SEP&gt;An OAuth grant mechanism combining an authorization code (issued upon user consent) and backend token exchange flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494595</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PKCE">
  <data key="d0">PKCE</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Proof Key for Code Exchange extension used to mitigate authorization code interception attacks on public clients.&lt;SEP&gt;Proof Key for Code Exchange; a extension that improves the security of the Authorization Code grant for public clients and confidential ones.&lt;SEP&gt;Proof Key for Code Exchange, a security layer built on the Authorization Code grant that strengthens token issuance, especially for public clients.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494596</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="OAuth Authorization Server">
  <data key="d0">OAuth Authorization Server</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">Server component responsible for validating authorization requests, issuing tokens, and controlling access decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;The server endpoint responsible for issuing authorization codes, handling token exchanges, and validating user consent.&lt;SEP&gt;Server responsible for managing OAuth authorization flows and granting access tokens to clients.&lt;SEP&gt;A server that issues access tokens and authorization codes based on an OAuth flow.&lt;SEP&gt;The server responsible for validating client credentials and issuing access tokens as part of the OAuth protocol flow.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-athz-05-1-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-athz-05-2-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785494560</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Code Verifier">
  <data key="d0">Code Verifier</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">Plaintext input field used to derive the `code_challenge` value in PKCE exchange, reused across multiple requests for a session.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-004</data>
