  <data key="d2">A short-lived token issued by the authorization server to access protected resources on behalf of the user.&lt;SEP&gt;A token produced by the authorization server after code exchange, permitting the client to access protected resources on behalf of the user.&lt;SEP&gt;A token issued by the authorization server after successful client authentication, granting permission to invoke protected APIs.&lt;SEP&gt;Bearer-level credential used by the client to access protected resources in place of the user's credentials.&lt;SEP&gt;A credential issued by the Authorization Server that clients present to the Resource Server to request access to protected resources.</data>
