  <data key="d3">doc-f381850f068d5b79abeb8a970d52c486-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1b26bd7d333a38ea2e920cfcff406e89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-35af4670be2579d771f8aacc9dfbff92-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d2">CSRF token validation prevents unauthorized state-changing requests from malicious origins.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness in session management where an attacker forces an authenticated user's browser to send unintended requests to a web application.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class where an attacker forces an authenticated user to execute unintended actions on a web application using the user's session credentials.</data>
