<node id="Browser Storage">
  <data key="d0">Browser Storage</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">A condition where tokens are stored in browser storage such as localStorage or sessionStorage due to client-side execution.&lt;SEP&gt;Client-side browser storage mechanisms such as localStorage or sessionStorage where credentials and tokens may be improperly saved.&lt;SEP&gt;An umbrella term for client-side storage mechanisms including localStorage, sessionStorage, and IndexedDB.&lt;SEP&gt;Client-side storage (such as localStorage) that can reveal stored assets if security controls are absent.&lt;/description&gt;</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-7d44ae2e3796fb2811788a45b296b379-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-566bc938b8c6a8464007d93896a672d4-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0ebda215dbd761aff6a4d8bfb5c054ba-chunk-002</data>
