<node id="Public Client">
  <data key="d0">Public Client</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackerCapability</data>
  <data key="d2">Type of Client that cannot protect secret information and is typically associated with frontend applications such as SPAs and mobile apps.&lt;SEP&gt;A client (e.g., frontend/spa/mobile) that cannot securely store credentials and requests access tokens without secrets.&lt;SEP&gt;A client application with limited capabilities to securely store secrets (often in-browser).</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-432cbf8013fe1cec9f0bb28ca6062ff9-chunk-000</data>
