<node id="Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS)">
  <data key="d0">Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS)</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">A browser policy mechanism that enables or restricts cross-domain requests and responses within a web application.&lt;SEP&gt;The web browser and server mechanism that enables cross-domain requests through XMLHttpRequest and HTTP headers while enforcing a security policy.&lt;SEP&gt;A browser-server protocol using HTTP headers to manage cross-domain access control for web resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Web protocol mechanism historically misconfigured to permit unauthorized cross-origin access to data resources.&lt;SEP&gt;A server policy that relaxes Same-Origin Policy restrictions for web resources to enable cross-origin requests programmatically.&lt;SEP&gt;A web protocol mechanism that influences session-related API responses and might interact with multi-session workflows.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a331af288c84a3d43384e1ec0cd67904-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d89410974592b19e283a445bd3ea68aa-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d89410974592b19e283a445bd3ea68aa-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6cdc807870a77b5064fef34c66d10a7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-f6cdc807870a77b5064fef34c66d10a7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0494a6f833c36d4bb797a335271d7b57-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-06-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-07-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-clnt-13-methodology.md&lt;SEP&gt;wstg-sess-11-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785584186</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
