<node id="Client-Side Resource Manipulation Vulnerability">
  <data key="d0">Client-Side Resource Manipulation Vulnerability</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">Input validation flaw where user-controlled data specifies the path or source of a loadable client-side resource, making injection or unauthorized content loading possible.&lt;SEP&gt;Weakness in input validation where user-supplied data determines the path or source of a loadable resource, leading to injection or unauthorized access.`&lt;SEP&gt;Input validation flaw that allows user-controlled data to specify resource paths, leading to injection or unauthorized content loading.`</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a331af288c84a3d43384e1ec0cd67904-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-06-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785497556</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Origin Header">
  <data key="d0">Origin Header</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">Client-sent HTTP header specifying the origin of a request, used by the browser to enforce cross-origin policy.&lt;SEP&gt;A browser-origin header always sent with cross-origin requests that specifies the domain initiating the request.&lt;SEP&gt;An HTTP field in the initial WebSocket handshake containing the origin of the connection request, used by servers to restrict cross-origin access.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d89410974592b19e283a445bd3ea68aa-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d89410974592b19e283a445bd3ea68aa-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6357b0935e2602236d9174d0c502b68b-chunk-000</data>
