</node>
<node id="ActionScript 3.0">
  <data key="d0">ActionScript 3.0</data>
  <data key="d1">TechnologyStack</data>
  <data key="d2">The newer version of the ActionScript language that includes the `navigateToURL` function for controlling a browser window from within Flash content.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbf0208722534d321dede8c097bd3086-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-08-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785497857</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unfiltered FlashVars input">
  <data key="d0">Unfiltered FlashVars input</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A flaw where FlashVars initial parameters are not properly validated or sanitized before being passed to dangerous functions like `getURL` or `navigateToURL`.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbf0208722534d321dede8c097bd3086-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-08-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785497857</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unvalidated `asfunction` parameter">
  <data key="d0">Unvalidated `asfunction` parameter</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness in Flash Player versions where the `asfunction` method allows arbitrary ActionScript code execution if the input lacks restrictions or allow-list validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbf0208722534d321dede8c097bd3086-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-08-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785497857</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unsafe `GetURL` usage">
  <data key="d0">Unsafe `GetURL` usage</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">An action that passes uncontrolled input directly into the `getURL` function call to exploit improper input validation or host-poisoning behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbf0208722534d321dede8c097bd3086-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-08-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785497857</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Unsafe `navigateToURL` usage">
  <data key="d0">Unsafe `navigateToURL` usage</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">An action that passes untrusted parameters or values to the `navigateToURL` function, allowing attacker-controlled URIs to be loaded in the browser window.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbf0208722534d321dede8c097bd3086-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-08-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785497857</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Cross Site Flashing (CSF)">
  <data key="d0">Cross Site Flashing (CSF)</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A type of client-side attack where malicious Flash content hosted on one site invades the context of another site using insecure embedding practices and browser automation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbf0208722534d321dede8c097bd3086-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-08-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785497857</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="ActionScript code execution">
  <data key="d0">ActionScript code execution</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">An action involving the execution of controlled ActionScript using functions such as `asfunction` when input is not adequately restricted or sourced from untrusted inputs.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbf0208722534d321dede8c097bd3086-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-clnt-08-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785497857</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
