<node id="unsafe-eval">
  <data key="d0">unsafe-eval</data>
  <data key="d1">PayloadPattern</data>
  <data key="d2">A Content-Security-Policy (CSP) directive setting that facilitates easier exploitation of template injection attacks by allowing dynamic code evaluation.&lt;SEP&gt;A CSP directive value that allows dynamic JavaScript evaluation via methods like `eval()`, `setTimeout(code)`, or `new Function()`, severely weakening policy security.&lt;SEP&gt;A CSP source value permitting JavaScript code evaluation via `eval()`, `Function`, or similar constructs, increasing bypass risk.&lt;SEP&gt;A CSP source value that permits dynamic code evaluation via functions like JavaScript `eval()`, drastically increasing the risk of bypassing security policies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-157a4cb1972bdf9a0880f5cf18f04a6a-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3ef7e3d50def7213b8e53e2fc6ca96f9-chunk-001</data>
