<node id="Subdomain">
  <data key="d0">Subdomain</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A lower-level domain name extension (e.g., subdomain.victim.com) within the main domain used as a target for takeover.&lt;SEP&gt;A domain component below a primary domain name (e.g., www.victim.com) whose DNS resolution to external services can be hijacked if the resource disappears and the DNS record is not cleaned up.&lt;SEP&gt;DNS level subdivision such as `hacker.app.mydomain.com`.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c13f010c37aa825f16fd20fc693f2648-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-c13f010c37aa825f16fd20fc693f2648-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-001</data>
