<node id="robots.txt">
  <data key="d0">robots.txt</data>
  <data key="d1">PreconditionEnvironment</data>
  <data key="d2">A configuration file at the web root that instructs web crawlers which pages or resources to exclude from crawling or indexing.&lt;SEP&gt;The plaintext file served from the web root that defines web spider/robot/crawler exclusions and indexing policies via the Robots Exclusion Protocol.&lt;SEP&gt;A textual file stored in the web server's web root directory that defines crawling and indexing rules for web spiders/robots/crawlers.&lt;SEP&gt;Contains directives such as Allow, Disallow, and Sitemap to control spider behavior for a website.&lt;SEP&gt;A robots.txt file served by a web server that may contain hints about directory structures or sensitive information.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-c8b308a52fdeb6c7f9a9a2dce9ca1cae-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-bef4f602c7766ccdd02613cff3449438-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1fdc50b475aa40c6258b79abf9a867a6-chunk-002</data>
