<node id="IP Address">
  <data key="d0">IP Address</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific numerical network address used as the subject for technical discovery techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;A specific network address used as a starting point for discovering hosted applications and services.&lt;SEP&gt;A numeric identifier assigned to a host on a local or network interface (e.g., 192.168.1.100) capable of hosting multiple web applications.Description: The network address which can be the target of port scanning and resolution to discover hidden services via DNS and virtual hosting.&lt;SEP&gt;An IPv4 or IPv6 address that can be associated with one or more DNS names in a 1-to-N relationship.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-af827feaaf7735b8242b6a751ee616fa-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-af827feaaf7735b8242b6a751ee616fa-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-af827feaaf7735b8242b6a751ee616fa-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-af827feaaf7735b8242b6a751ee616fa-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-af827feaaf7735b8242b6a751ee616fa-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-af827feaaf7735b8242b6a751ee616fa-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0494a6f833c36d4bb797a335271d7b57-chunk-002</data>
