  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness where applications handle multiple instances of the same HTTP request parameter unpredictably, affecting input processing and access control logic.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where multiple identical request parameters are concatenated in the application layer, bypassing server-side input filtering.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where multiple values assigned to the same input parameter impact application logic due to lack of proper parameter separation or validation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-3be59af692385f8910776899901b815f-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3be59af692385f8910776899901b815f-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-3be59af692385f8910776899901b815f-chunk-000</data>
