  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness in the application allowing arbitrary SQL commands to be injected and executed.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness in web applications where user input is improperly constrained before being concatenated into SQL queries, allowing arbitrary database access and command execution.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class where user input is improperly sanitized and incorporated directly into SQL queries, allowing malicious execution.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness in input validation allowing execution of SQL statements through user input.</data>
