<node id="SSI Injection">
  <data key="d0">SSI Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">AttackTechnique</data>
  <data key="d2">A testing action injecting Server-Side Includes (SSI) directives as user-supplied input to determine if the server executes them without proper validation.SSI directives that are injected into user input fields and interpreted by the web server due to incomplete validation.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness type where attacker-controlled input is interpreted as Server-Side Include directives by the web server.&lt;SEP&gt;A testing or attack action to inject malicious SSI directives into input fields of a web application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-8572f501a826eda55dfbb3563ca66b07-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8572f501a826eda55dfbb3563ca66b07-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-8572f501a826eda55dfbb3563ca66b07-chunk-002</data>
