<node id="Format String Injection">
  <data key="d0">Format String Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness class where server-side code concatenates user input with a format string that interprets conversion specifiers at runtime, leading to information disclosure or potentially code execution depending on the language and use of modifiers like `%n`.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class where user controlled input containing conversion specifiers is passed directly to string formatting functions without sanitization.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where unsanitized user input is appended to a format string argument in server-side code, leading to information disclosure, crashes, or memory corruption depending on the language and specifiers used.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness where application code uses user-controlled format specifiers without validation, potentially causing crashes, data leakage, or code execution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-94f308342598cce2ab79e26439b43b5f-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-94f308342598cce2ab79e26439b43b5f-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-94f308342598cce2ab79e26439b43b5f-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-94f308342598cce2ab79e26439b43b5f-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-inpv-13-13-testing-for-format-string-injection-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785582238</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
