<node id="CSV Injection">
  <data key="d0">CSV Injection</data>
  <data key="d1">VulnerabilityClass</data>
  <data key="d2">A weakness where input is not properly validated or sanitized, allowing injection of spreadsheet formulas or commands into CSV data that become active when opened in spreadsheet applications.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class where untrusted user input is embedded into CSV files in a way that spreadsheet applications interpret it as formulas upon opening.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness in web applications where untrusted user input embedded in CSV exports is treated as formulas when opened in spreadsheet applications, enabling deception or further exploitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-1fdef32ca149cd0b391b755204dc40b2-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1fdef32ca149cd0b391b755204dc40b2-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-1fdef32ca149cd0b391b755204dc40b2-chunk-002</data>
