<node id="SameSite=Strict">
  <data key="d0">SameSite=Strict</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A specific SameSite cookie attribute value that restricts cookie transmission to first-party context only per browser URL bar.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-02-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SameSite=Lax">
  <data key="d0">SameSite=Lax</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A SameSite cookie attribute value that is less restrictive than Strict, sending the cookie with first-party requests even from third-party source links.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-02-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583397</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="SameSite=None">
  <data key="d0">SameSite=None</data>
  <data key="d1">DefensiveControl</data>
  <data key="d2">A SameSite cookie attribute value that sends the cookie in all contexts (cross-site included), mandating the Secure attribute otherwise ignored by modern browsers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">wstg-sess-02-methodology.md</data>
  <data key="d5">1785583397</data>
