<node id="Session Management Testing">
  <data key="d0">Session Management Testing</data>
  <data key="d1">Artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">WSTG category focused on session integrity and cookie security controls&lt;SEP&gt;Objective to test and identify weaknesses in session identifier handling, exposure, and security.&lt;SEP&gt;A weakness class focused on improper handling of user sessions that permits unauthorized impersonation.&lt;SEP&gt;The overarching security discipline focused on ensuring user sessions are correctly created, used, and terminated according to policy.&lt;SEP&gt;The category under which WSTG-SESS-08 is classified within the Web Security Testing Guide framework.&lt;SEP&gt;Testing domain focused on session-based authentication and authorization mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;WSTG category that groups web application security test scenarios related to session handling and control.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-0b5d4912d9dca5c18a19c922b0e93be4-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2138db10de64fa713c14c45b2f2d6483-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2138db10de64fa713c14c45b2f2d6483-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-0a3e9e7d3b55a0f4286d2a3f106f4013-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-83827c52b87edd7a3b3969c34753607b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-83827c52b87edd7a3b3969c34753607b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a94663073c0acb859206ca0011ed60dc-chunk-004</data>
